{
 "manufacturer": "DEIF",
 "manufacturer_slug": "deif",
 "model": "SGC 120 / SGC 121 Single Genset Controller",
 "model_slug": "sgc-120-sgc-121",
 "short_model": "SGC 120/121",
 "aliases": [
  "SGC 120",
  "SGC 121",
  "SGC120",
  "SGC121"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Generator controller",
 "applies_to": "SGC 120 and SGC 121 (first generation, not Mk II); the SGC 120 user manual 4189341340B covers application software 9.04.",
 "summary": "The SGC 120 and SGC 121 are DEIF's small auto-start and AMF genset controllers. They act as a Modbus RTU server on one RS-485 port, and every value is a holding register read with function 03. This map covers the 16-bit generator, mains and load readings, engine values, start and trip counters, the packed alarm-state, I/O and genset-status words, and the mode-change command.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "0-based",
  "note": "The tables print plain register numbers starting at 0, and the user manual's frame layouts put the register address from the map straight into the request. Read generator L1-N voltage at 1, not 40002."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": "Application software 9.04 (user manual 4189341340B)",
 "source": {
  "title": "SGC 120 and SGC 121 Modbus tables",
  "doc_number": "4189341357",
  "revision_date": null,
  "url": "https://deif-cdn-umbraco.azureedge.net/media/pawhllhf/sgc-120-sgc-121-modbus-tables-4189341357.xlsx",
  "pages": "Spreadsheet sheet 'Holding register (03;16)'; RS-485 settings in SGC 120 user manual 4189341340B ch. 7, pp. 65-66"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Left out: the 32-bit energy counters (39-50) and engine run hours (60-61). The tables give each as a two-register range with no word order, so they cannot be decoded with certainty.",
  "Scaling is a multiplier: 0.1 means the raw value is in tenths.",
  "Alarm words 65-76 each pack four alarms as 4-bit fields. The table numbers bits 1-16 and puts the first-listed alarm in bits 13-16, the next in 9-12, then 5-8 and 1-4. It does not say whether bit 1 is the least significant bit, so the fields are not split here. Each field holds 0 = disabled, 1 = not active, 2 = warning, 3 = shutdown, 4 = electrical trip, 5 = notification.",
  "Word 77 packs digital inputs A-I (table bits 16 down to 8) and outputs A-F (bits 7 down to 2). Word 78 packs, from table bit 16 down: SGC mode, mains healthy, operation mode (bits 14-12: 110 scheduler, 101 auto, 100 manual), load on mains, load on DG, DG running/stopped, stopped normally, stopped with fault, fail to start, gen available, common shutdown, common electric trip, common warning, common notification. The same bit-numbering caveat applies.",
  "Registers 79-81 hold the time stamp as packed hex bytes (minute/second, weekday/hour, month/day) and are not listed; 82 holds the year.",
  "Mode-change writes use function 16 to register 0 with one key code at a time.",
  "RS-485 settings come from the SGC 120 user manual 4189341340B (https://deif-cdn-umbraco.azureedge.net/media/1ajpbyvp/sgc-120-user-manual-4189341340-uk.pdf)."
 ],
